# web_app: commit and push

After changing any file under `web_app/`, commit and push before finishing the task.

## When to run

- Any edit, add, or delete under `web_app/` (static files, API, config, etc.)
- Skip if the session only read files or made no `web_app/` changes

## Workflow

1. `git status` and `git diff` — confirm only intended `web_app/` changes are included
2. Stage `web_app/` changes (do not stage secrets: `.env`, credentials)
3. Commit with a short message focused on why (1–2 sentences)
4. Push to the current branch (`git push` or `git push -u origin HEAD` if no upstream)

## Commit message

Match repo style. Examples:

- `fix(web_app): remove stale reload button handler`
- `refactor(web_app): simplify profile section header`

## Constraints

- Do not amend, force-push, or skip hooks unless the user explicitly asks
- Do not push to `main`/`master` with force
- If push fails (auth, conflicts), report the error and what was committed locally
